rules.message:
Prisma 6 returns `Uint8Array` instead of Node.js `Buffer` for `Bytes` fields.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Prisma 5)
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { id: 1 } });
const hex = user.avatar.toString('hex'); // Assumes Buffer

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6)
const user = await prisma.user.findUniqueOrThrow({ where: { id: 1 } });
// Convert Uint8Array to Buffer if Node buffer methods are required:
const hex = Buffer.from(user.avatar).toString('hex');
```
</details>

`NotFoundError` export has been removed from `@prisma/client` in Prisma 6. Check for error code `'P2025'`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Prisma 5)
import { NotFoundError } from '@prisma/client';
if (err instanceof NotFoundError) { /* handle 404 */ }

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6)
import { Prisma } from '@prisma/client';
if (err instanceof Prisma.PrismaClientKnownRequestError && err.code === 'P2025') {
  /* handle 404 */
}
```
</details>

`rejectOnNotFound` option has been removed in Prisma 6. Use `findUniqueOrThrow()` or `findFirstOrThrow()`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { id: 1 },
  rejectOnNotFound: true
});

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6)
const user = await prisma.user.findUniqueOrThrow({
  where: { id: 1 }
});
```
</details>

`prisma.$use()` middleware is deprecated in Prisma 6. Migrate to Client Extensions using `prisma.$extends()`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Legacy $use middleware)
prisma.$use(async (params, next) => {
  const before = Date.now();
  const result = await next(params);
  console.log(`Query took ${Date.now() - before}ms`);
  return result;
});

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6 $extends)
const prisma = new PrismaClient().$extends({
  query: {
    $allModels: {
      async $allOperations({ operation, args, query }) {
        const before = Date.now();
        const result = await query(args);
        console.log(`Query took ${Date.now() - before}ms`);
        return result;
      }
    }
  }
});
```
</details>

remediation.exampleAfter:
const xprisma = prisma.$extends({
  query: { $allModels: { async $allOperations({ query, args }) { return query(args); } } }
});

rules.message:
Prefer parameterized `$executeRaw` or `$queryRaw` tagged template literals over `$executeRawUnsafe`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Unsafe raw query)
await prisma.$executeRawUnsafe(`UPDATE users SET status = '${status}' WHERE id = ${id}`);

// ✅ AFTER (Safe parameterized raw query)
await prisma.$executeRaw`UPDATE users SET status = ${status} WHERE id = ${id}`;
```
</details>

`driverAdapters` preview feature is GA in Prisma 6 and no longer needed in `previewFeatures`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```prisma
// ❌ BEFORE (Prisma 5)
generator client {
  provider        = "prisma-client-js"
  previewFeatures = ["driverAdapters"]
}

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6)
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}
```
</details>

`relationJoins` is now Generally Available in Prisma 6 and does not require previewFeatures.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```prisma
// ❌ BEFORE
previewFeatures = ["relationJoins"]

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6)
// Removed 'relationJoins'
```
</details>

`jsonProtocol` is default in Prisma 6 and should be removed from `previewFeatures`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```prisma
// ❌ BEFORE
previewFeatures = ["jsonProtocol"]

// ✅ AFTER (Prisma 6)
// Removed 'jsonProtocol'
```
</details>
